# net-snmp's snmp_shutdown() does not free the MIB tree buckets that
# init_snmp() allocates, so every init and shutdown pair leaks them. The
# allocation and the loss are both inside libnetsnmp.
{
   net-snmp MIB tree buckets survive snmp_shutdown
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:calloc
   fun:netsnmp_init_mib_internals
}
